      "level": 3,
      "content": "Irrigation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "st1elpj",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh has significant irrigation infrastructure. The major sources of irrigation include canals, tanks, and tubewells. The major irrigation projects include the Chambal Irrigation Project (serving MP and Rajasthan), the Tawa Project (Hoshangabad), Bargi Dam (on Narmada, Jabalpur), Bansagar Dam (on Son River, Shahdol), and Indira Sagar Dam (world's largest capacity reservoir, Khandwa)."
    },
    {
      "id": "glkxnlm",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Indira Sagar Dam - On Narmada at Punasa, Khandwa - Largest reservoir in India by capacity (12.22 BCM)",
        "Omkareshwar Dam - On Narmada, Khandwa district - Hydropower project",
        "Bargi Dam (Rani Avanti Bai Lodhi Sagar) - On Narmada, Jabalpur",
        "Tawa Dam - On Tawa River (tributary of Narmada), Hoshangabad",
        "Bansagar Dam - On Son River, Shahdol - Multi-purpose project",
        "Gandhi Sagar Dam - On Chambal River, Mandsaur"
      ]
    },
